---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="What TV Tattler is, how it is put together, and the reference-first approach behind it."
>
  <article class="page">
    <header class="page__header">
      <p class="mono page__kicker">About</p>
      <h1>About TV Tattler</h1>
      <p class="page__standfirst">
        TV Tattler is an independent UK entertainment site covering the nation&rsquo;s
        favourite soaps — EastEnders, Coronation Street, Emmerdale and Hollyoaks — plus
        the wider world of telly and film. We pair a well-maintained reference archive with
        original spoilers, features and what&rsquo;s-on guides.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="page__body">
      <h2>What we do</h2>
      <p>
        We do two things. First, we keep a genuine <strong>reference archive</strong> — a
        proper, maintained page for every show, character and actor, complete with portrayal
        timelines and family connections. Second, we publish <strong>original writing</strong>:
        weekly spoilers, cast news, character guides and features, written in our own words.
        The archive is what people come back to; the articles keep it fresh.
      </p>

      <h2>Who runs it</h2>
      <p>
        TV Tattler is an independent publication, written and maintained by
        <strong>Shaun Russett</strong> with a small editorial team. It is not affiliated with
        the BBC, ITV, Channel 4, or any broadcaster or production company. Show, character and
        cast names are used for reference and commentary only.
      </p>

      <h2>Our editorial standards</h2>
      <ul class="standards">
        <li><strong>Facts first.</strong> Reference pages are only worth keeping if they are right, so we check what we publish and flag anything uncertain rather than guess.</li>
        <li><strong>Our own words.</strong> We write our articles ourselves. When we cover a spoiler or story another outlet has reported, we credit and link to them under Sources &mdash; we never copy their text.</li>
        <li><strong>Spoilers are signposted.</strong> Spoiler articles carry a clear warning so you can choose whether to read on.</li>
        <li><strong>Editorial reviewing.</strong> Pages are compiled from public reference data and reviewed by our editors before they go live.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Corrections &amp; feedback</h2>
      <p>
        We want the archive to be accurate. If you spot something wrong, out of date, or
        missing, please tell us at
        <a href="mailto:editor@tvtattler.com">editor@tvtattler.com</a> and we&rsquo;ll review
        and fix it promptly. Tips and suggestions are welcome too.
      </p>

      <h2>Advertising</h2>
      <p>
        TV Tattler is free to read and supported by advertising, which lets us keep it that
        way. Ads are clearly separated from our editorial content and never influence what we
        write. For how advertising cookies work and the choices you have, see our
        <a href="/privacy/">privacy &amp; cookies policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Where our information comes from</h2>
      <p>
        Our facts and articles are our own, checked and written up here. Some open data helps
        keep the automatic pages fresh, and we credit it as those sources ask:
      </p>
      <ul class="credits">
        <li>
          Cast and show facts draw on <a href="https://www.wikidata.org" rel="external nofollow">Wikidata</a>
          (public domain), with any photos credited to their author and licence on the
          page they appear.
        </li>
        <li>
          Upcoming-episode air dates use data from
          <a href="https://www.tvmaze.com" rel="external nofollow">TVmaze</a> (CC&nbsp;BY-SA).
        </li>
        <li>
          Cinema-release listings use
          <a href="https://www.themoviedb.org" rel="external nofollow">The Movie Database (TMDB)</a>.
          This product uses the TMDB API but is not endorsed or certified by TMDB.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Corrections, tips, advertising and general enquiries:
        <a href="mailto:editor@tvtattler.com">editor@tvtattler.com</a>. You can also read our
        <a href="/privacy/">privacy &amp; cookies policy</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page {
    max-width: 44rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }
  .page__header {
    border-bottom: 4px solid var(--live);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-4);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-5);
  }
  .page__kicker {
    color: var(--ink-40);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }
  .page__standfirst {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    color: var(--ink-80);
  }
  .page__body :global(h2) {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }
  .page__body p {
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }
  .page__body a {
    text-decoration-color: var(--live);
    text-decoration-thickness: 2px;
  }
  .page__body :global(ul.standards),
  .page__body :global(ul.credits) {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    padding-left: 1.1rem;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-2);
  }
  .page__body :global(ul.standards li),
  .page__body :global(ul.credits li) {
    color: var(--ink-80);
  }
</style>
